  "caption": "Betrayal has turned you into a person who values peace over big circles , fake vibes & weird smiles 😭😭\n\n1on1 calls link in bio",
  "transcript": {
    "text": "Betrayal turned you into an introvert. You're not antisocial when you know how to socialize. You're just selective because you understand what access can cost you. And after enough disappointment, protecting your peace starts making more sense than proving you're friendly. There's so many pretenders and low-key haters that sometimes it's easier to stay to yourself, than it give opportunities to people to create situations that you didn't even ask for. And for some people, the first betrayal wasn't even from a stranger, it was probably from family members that they loved, defended, and protected. The friends they stood beside during their lowest moments, suddenly became impossible to reach when they needed support in return. Sometimes the people closest to you aren't always the safest people to trust. Not everybody asking to be close to you is coming to support you. Some people are coming to use you, to study you, to collect information, to compare themselves to you, or to look for ways to benefit from having access to your life. That's why being private isn't always about being bitter. Sometimes it's about being wiser. Now there's a new appreciation for staying out the mix, keeping small circles, and protecting your peace.",
